      "title": "Implement Markdown Content Processing",
      "description": "Set up utilities to read and parse Markdown blog posts from the `gatsby/content/blog` directory.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [
        2
      ],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "1. Install necessary libraries: `gray-matter`, `remark`, `remark-html`.\n2. Create utility functions in `src/lib/posts.ts` (or similar) to:\n   - Read files from `gatsby/content/blog`.\n   - Parse frontmatter using `gray-matter`.\n   - Convert Markdown content to HTML using `remark`.\n   - Generate slugs from filenames (e.g., removing date prefixes).",
      "testStrategy": "Write unit tests for the utility functions. Test reading a sample Markdown file and verify correct parsing of frontmatter and HTML content generation.",
      "subtasks": []
    },
    {
