    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Migrate Global CSS to Tailwind Utility Classes",
      "description": "Extract and migrate styles from globals.css to inline Tailwind CSS classes across all components, following Tailwind v4 best practices.",
      "details": "This task involves a systematic migration from global CSS to Tailwind utility classes:\n\n1. **Audit Phase**:\n   - Create an inventory of all styles in src/app/globals.css\n   - Categorize styles into: layout, typography, colors, animations, responsive styles, etc.\n   - Identify which styles have direct Tailwind equivalents and which might need theme extensions\n\n2. **Migration Planning**:\n   - Create a mapping document that shows each global CSS rule and its Tailwind equivalent\n   - Identify components affected by each global style\n   - Determine if any styles need to be maintained as CSS variables in the Tailwind config\n\n3. **Implementation**:\n   - Update the Tailwind config to include any necessary theme extensions\n   - Systematically update each component to use Tailwind classes instead of relying on globals.css\n   - For complex styles without direct Tailwind equivalents, use the @apply directive in component-specific CSS modules\n   - For repeated patterns, consider creating Tailwind component classes in the config\n\n4. **Cleanup**:\n   - Remove migrated styles from globals.css\n   - Verify no component styling breaks after removal\n   - Consolidate any remaining necessary global styles\n\n5. **Documentation**:\n   - Document any custom Tailwind extensions added to the config\n   - Update component documentation to reflect the new styling approach\n\nEnsure backward compatibility throughout the migration process by implementing and testing changes incrementally.",
      "testStrategy": "To verify successful migration:\n\n1. **Visual Regression Testing**:\n   - Take screenshots of key UI components before migration\n   - Compare with post-migration screenshots to ensure visual consistency\n   - Test across multiple viewport sizes to verify responsive behavior\n\n2. **Component Testing**:\n   - Create a checklist of components affected by globals.css\n   - Verify each component renders correctly with Tailwind classes\n   - Test component states (hover, focus, active, disabled) to ensure all styles are properly migrated\n\n3. **Browser Compatibility**:\n   - Test in Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge to ensure cross-browser compatibility\n   - Verify mobile rendering on iOS and Android devices\n\n4. **Performance Checks**:\n   - Compare bundle sizes before and after migration\n   - Measure CSS specificity improvements\n   - Verify reduced CSS file size after removing globals.css\n\n5. **Validation Steps**:\n   - Run the application with globals.css completely removed to verify no styling dependencies remain\n   - Use browser dev tools to confirm styles are applied via Tailwind classes\n   - Verify no unexpected CSS cascading issues occur\n   - Check for any console errors related to missing styles",
      "status": "pending",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "high"
    }
